## Verified bounded functionality

`src/FFPerformanceEngine.Core/Services/GenericGuardianWindowsProcessLifetimeProbe.cs` observes a real Windows process handle: positive exact PID, fully qualified expected executable, actual `MainModule.FileName`, OS `Process.StartTime` converted UTC, and no exit before/after the read. On mismatch, process exit, missing/access-denied metadata or non-Windows OS it returns unavailable, never guessed proof. Its snapshot has an internal constructor and no public mutator; `IsStillSameProcess` reopens the physical process and checks PID, path and creation timestamp. Test runs against the real Windows CI selftest process, checks stable repeated observation, nonexistent PID, wrong path, missing and relative path. It does NOT identify a real game's scene, assign the Guardian host session Guid, claim causality, mutate Windows or wire itself into the canary executor.

## Source feasibility audit, no invented scene evidence

Read `Workloads/GameAdapterFramework.cs`: `GenericGameAdapter` exposes no game-specific capabilities; `BlueStacksFreeFireGameAdapter` declares state/config/benchmark/telemetry capabilities but NO scene/mode/load verification. `Workloads/GameEvidenceModels.cs`, `GameEvidenceBinder.cs`, `RunningProcessGameEvidenceSource.cs`: running process and launcher evidence bind stable game identity, not internal game scenes; the running-process observation supplies PID/path/observation time but no start time until this separate probe. `Services/BlueStacksAutomationService.cs`: ADB window query can recognise the Free Fire foreground Android package, not gameplay scene. `Services/BlueStacksAutoTunerRuntime.cs`: preparation waits for foreground and PresentMon captures performance, not scene/load equivalence. `Telemetry/TelemetryFrame.cs` holds timestamp/metric observations/quality, no scene/mode/load. `Services/GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor.cs` currently accepts `IGenericGuardianCanaryEvidenceSource` injection but no real production implementation is registered. The current comparison is structurally fail-closed if source absent; a test-only source is not a production proof. This is a targeted code inspection, not a claim to have independently reverse-engineered game internals.

## Boundary and next action

The new OS proof covers only PHYSICAL PROCESS CONTINUITY and PID reuse; it is a standalone observer. Real gameplay scene/mode/load/environment, external benchmark interference and other unrelated mutations remain unproven. Track0 process-local activity generation is observational, not mutual exclusion. No actual game HIL or claimed FPS gain. Generic Guardian remains OFF, specialized FF/BlueStacks unchanged, no startup discovery or history promotion.

Next: integrate the concrete OS process lifetime proof at the host/canary boundary with TDD and preserve existing synthetic selftests by explicitly separating test-only dependencies, without allowing a fake probe to grant production authority. Then investigate an explicitly supported game adapter's legitimate scene/mode/load source; absent genuine APIs/instrumentation remain Unknown and no mutations. Add external/other-mutation observers only where truthful. Finally design owner-managed host with session epoch, trusted action catalog, budget, global benchmark exclusion, exact kept-lease cleanup and Windows/HIL before auto activation. Track6 item3 IN PROGRESS; items4/5 pending.
